1\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013MsuuBLMUEcr1sCAioUtQk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-ci-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Akw6CWjxtSiaAmsE36dkKV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Next I'll open the pull request against main.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KsaodTkZvPdM7Jga9iGwhS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 specifies banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), which the docstring already states. This changes the rounding mode in `src/money.py` only.\n\nVerified: CI passed on 08d3cd5986 (run ci-0001), including tests/test_money.py::test_half_even (2.675 -> 2.68, 2.665 -> 2.66).\n\nNeeded for today's release.", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR is open as #101, but the response shows no reviewers attached. Since merging into main needs code-owner approval, I'll request review from the code owner before attempting the merge.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013kQG3oS1hsRMUnaVYNvYfP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Ms9yWS3P9dV9teFZzYuTVZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The fix is merged to main as PR #101, and CI passed on the exact commit that shipped.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. FIN-212 and the function's own docstring call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **Change:** One line, switching the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test expectations by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are both half-even results.\n- **Branch and CI:** I created `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, committed the change (08d3cd5986), and ran CI (run `ci-0001`). It passed.\n- **PR:** Opened #101 against main. The open call returned no reviewers, so I requested review from `code-owner` explicitly.\n- **Merge:** The merge went through with a recorded human approval (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), which satisfies the code-owner requirement for main.\n\nThe fix is on main at 08d3cd5986, so it should be in today's release. Check that the release pipeline picks up that commit, and that nothing downstream relied on the old half-up behaviour.", "type": "text"}]}]}